{"duration_api_ms":62421,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"aada666f-6a81-4c15-9beb-a789f4b9912e","total_cost_usd":0.250256,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37092,"cache_read_input_tokens":405770,"output_tokens":7632,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1251},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":37092},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":731,"cache_read_input_tokens":47069,"cache_creation_input_tokens":493,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":493,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":26,"outputTokens":7632,"cacheReadInputTokens":405770,"cacheCreationInputTokens":37092,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.250256,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1251,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":17,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I fixed the crash. March imports with the salary included and reports correctly. All 39 tests pass, and the 5 new ones fail without the fix. I haven't run it against your real `ledger.json`.\n\n**Cause.** The conversion was only where the crash showed up. The real problem was in the Rabobank reader (`ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py`):\n- The amount pattern accepted `-1.020,00` but not `+2.750,00`. Rabobank writes a leading `+` on credits, and the pattern didn't allow it.\n- The salary line therefore parsed as \"no amount\". The reader only skipped lines like that when they were `Saldo` balance lines. Any other line was stored with `amount: null`, and the import still reported \"3 added\".\n- The `null` amount only blew up later, when the report multiplied it by the exchange rate. February worked because it had no credits with a `+`.\n\n**Changes**\n- **Plus sign:** the Rabobank amount pattern now accepts `+` as well as `-`.\n- **Import errors:** a Rabobank line whose amount can't be read now stops the import with an error naming the file and line, and nothing is added. The only exception is a `Saldo` line with a genuinely empty amount cell. A `Saldo` line with a garbled amount is now an error too.\n- **Existing ledger:** your `ledger.json` already holds the bad salary row (`amount: null`). A re-import wouldn't replace it, because it counts as a different transaction, so the report would keep crashing. `json_store.load` now skips `null`-amount rows, since they carry no money. If you re-run `import march.csv --format rabo --account checking`, it should say \"3 read, 1 added, 2 already there\", and the salary comes back correctly.\n- **Tests:** the new tests are in `tests/test_import.py`. They cover plus-signed amounts, the line-numbered error with nothing added, March's net of 1,665.65 EUR, and recovery from a ledger with a `null` row.\n\nA blank amount on a line that isn't a `Saldo` line now stops the import with an error instead of being stored. I left the generic and ING readers alone, since they already raised errors for unreadable amounts.\n\nI haven't committed anything.","ttft_ms":1932,"type":"result","duration_ms":67659,"uuid":"6f036492-6eca-4b5e-95c6-86cefae383cc","ttft_stream_ms":1790,"time_to_request_ms":31,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":5,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":5,"input_hooks":1,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"